WEBVTT

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:06.630
Masazumi? I haven't seen you since middle school.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:07.820
Who're you?

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.360
Are you really Futayo?

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.990
You dare interfere?

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:15.040
Who is the one really interfering here?

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.900
What is it?

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.580
Hey, whoa! If it isn't Ic and Mrs. Ic!

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:23.830
You two on a walk?

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.460
Don't be insolent!

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.020
Ic am King of Musashi, Yoshinao!

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.460
[Yoshinao uses "maro", a very old term, to refer to himself.
"Ic", the Old English for "I,"]

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.460
Ic have come to stop your outrage!

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.630
Pope President,

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.510
Ic would like Galileo to take his leave.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.510
<i>Oh, and if he doesn't?</i>

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.790
<i>King of Musashi, you are not a student,</i>

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:44.060
<i>so you cannot interfere with student contention.</i>

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.470
That dame is captain of my guard.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.650
She has trained under Tadakatsu Honda

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.500
and possesses the prototype for
an Armor of Deadly Sins,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.150
the Divine Weapon, Slicing Dragonfly.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.760
Ic would like to see if any of these kids can defeat her

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.370
as a form of remonstration.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.090
<i>Do you have any proof that show-off isn't in</i>

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.540
<i>cahoots with Musashi's students?</i>

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.250
Hey, Old Fart!

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:08.460
Don't put us in the same boat as that cosplay freak!

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.990
In other words, King Yoshinao,

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:14.630
you want one of us to fight Futayo?

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.090
Diving!

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.090
That's crazy!

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.580
Futayo's so strong...

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:20.140
Hey, hey, hey!

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:22.730
The Pope President may have intruded

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:25.200
upon Masazumi and Aoi's debate,

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.270
but I declare that both sides have valid stances.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:29.490
Is that acceptable?

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:32.480
<i>I will take care not to intrude again.</i>

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.490
Then, with one win, one loss and one tie,
we need a tiebreaker.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.720
Musashi will be facing off against...

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:45.910
Your blades will fall short of your
foes if ye cannot best me.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.510
Well? Who will face me?

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.270
Nani ga mieru?

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.270
What do you see?

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.690
Ari no mama no kimi wa

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.690
You've closed yourself off to love

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:21.580
Tsuyoku naru made itoshisa wo tojite

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:21.580
Until you grow innately strong

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.660
Nani wo kiku no?

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.660
What are you listening to?

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.750
Himitsu no kobeya de

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.750
Shall I tell you about days long past

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:33.590
Inishie no hibi katarou ka?

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:33.590
In our secret little room?

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:36.800
Kioku ni dakarete

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:36.800
Embraced in memories

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.090
Kudakareta mysteria

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.090
The mysteria crumbles

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.850
Higeki wo koete

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.850
Once you overcome this tragedy

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.060
Odayaka na inori

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.060
Offer a gentle prayer

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:49.080
Owari ga hajimari

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:49.080
Endings are just beginnings

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.270
Shinsekai de hito wa mirai wo

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.270
People toss aside all they have

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.860
Bishu no you ni

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.860
Without ever knowing

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:58.330
Nomi hoseru ka sae shirazu

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:58.330
If they could drink up the new world

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:01.490
Subete houri nageta

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:01.490
Like a savory wine

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.650
Shinsekai wa tsumetai risei to

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.650
The new world resides

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.370
Kiseki no hazama

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.370
Between boring logic and miracles

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:16.380
Doushite koko de kimi to aeta no

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:16.380
I wonder why this is where I first met you

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:25.530
The Summit's Flower

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:27.470
As a knight, I should go "ka-boom!" and whack her.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.600
No, how 'bout I go "shmaash" with Jizuri Suzaku?

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:33.850
Or I could go "fu-whoosh" with a long-range attack.

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.700
Why do these women keep using onomatopoeia?

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.790
I should fight her!

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.910
But it would be over as soon as she squished you.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:42.910
Goodness!

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.030
And our spells take a while to prepare.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:46.280
In that case...

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.310
I guess that leaves me.

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:55.920
No, I should go up before you do, Sir Neshinbara.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.740
No, no way.

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:59.110
Not you, Tenzo.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:01.980
That woman uses an old style, formal speech.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.300
You don't take it quite as far as her, ya know?

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.830
You've lost in a battle of character
before you even fight!

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.980
Damn, y..you're right!

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.870
I have nothing in my defense.

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:16.900
Listen up, fools and foolish brother.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.610
Your ingenious big sister shall save your sorry butts.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.440
Ms. Boobless Politician, move it.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:24.830
It's dangerous here.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:28.400
Sis is scary if you don't do what she says.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.610
Will she be okay?

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.650
Yeah, she'll be just fine!

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.590
This is in my way.

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:47.540
<i>A warrior versus a strange woman?</i>

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:49.170
<i>Is this much of a fight?</i>

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:50.640
Hey, Ic-Ic!

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:54.140
If my sis wins, could you make me king?

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:58.810
What?! Why would Ic make you King of Musashi?

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.350
<i>He has no idea what Ic went through</i>

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:03.110
<i>when Ic became king of this realm!</i>

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:08.660
<i>Ic was the lord of a small country until then...</i>

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:10.610
<i>Curse the Testament Union!</i>

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.770
<i>They'll destroy my domain
if Ic don't become Musashi's king!</i>

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.810
<i>In order to protect my country and people,</i>

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.550
<i>Ic chose to become Musashi's king.</i>

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:22.760
What would you do if you became king?

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.450
Me?

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:28.490
I want to get back everything
Horizon lost because of me.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:35.780
Going by your attire, I take it you are a Shirabyoushi.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.570
I see you're a dreary woman ignorant of the arts.

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:40.980
This goes back much further.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:45.360
I am afraid I fail to appreciate the arts.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.400
You don't lead a corrupted life.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:49.700
How boring!

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.410
Uzzy, come out.

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:52.220
Asama Shrine

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.690
Yay, Uzzy!

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:58.210
This is the mouse for the
Head Deity of the Performing Arts, Uzume.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:00.880
Do you know about the Uzume-based deities?

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:05.240
All I know is that they spread emotions linked

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:06.590
to rowdiness and humor.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.680
Then, let me enlighten you.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:16.540
Just so you know, my contracts are

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.600
all related to erotica and dancing.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.230
You truly lack anything battle-related?

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.590
<i>I must exercise caution,</i>

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:28.820
<i>but all it will take is one hit to defeat her.</i>

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:31.950
<i>There's no need to sever her with Slicing Dragonfly.</i>

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:35.080
<i>I need to confirm something first: Her speed!</i>

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.040
En garde!

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:41.130
She's fast!

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.670
It's over.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.630
<i>Impossible! I can't believe reality lied!</i>

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:52.920
Don't waste our time on such a simple conclusion.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:56.620
Foolish brother, how are you supposed
to react at a time like this?

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:57.640
Go on, show us!

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:02.090
Wow, you're really cute!

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:04.050
You're so wet!

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:05.310
Bucket, oh, bucket!

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.350
He's flirting with a bucket...

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:09.490
Your brother is rather forward.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.740
I'll toss him into sewerage water later.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:18.980
As for you, the dullest woman in
the Far East, Futayo Honda,

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:20.660
your speed is wailing.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:20.660
Soaring Wings 
 Activated

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:26.310
Gotcha!

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:27.560
How crude.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:30.720
You must pluck a flower, not reap it.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:32.800
What was that spell?

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:37.010
Who's stupid enough to ask that
or stupid enough to answer?

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:39.640
But I'll brag!

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:41.890
Remember?

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:44.980
I said my contracts specialize
in erotica and dances.

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:48.690
But do you think being erotic means
I'm open to anyone?

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:54.450
My Summit Dance is a spell that
prevents thugs from touching me.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:08:00.450
The only ones who can touch me are
those I wish to wither away for.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.330
Now, give it a shot!

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:05.130
See if you can reach the summit.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:09.090
As long as I offer my ritual dances, I am the summit!

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:17.060
Toorimase, toorimase

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:17.060
Let us pass, let us pass

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:18.500
The Song of Passage?

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:20.220
She's turning it into a dance song.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:23.980
Toorimase, toorimase

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:23.980
Let us pass, let us pass

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:21.980
Damn!

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.380
<i>She's increasing the offering's value!</i>

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:26.230
Then, I'll have to pass through!

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:30.530
Toorimase, toorimase

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:30.530
Let us pass, let us pass

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:30.190
Summit Dance

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:35.640
Ikaba izuko ga hosomichi nareba

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:35.640
Where doth this narrow path lead?

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:41.500
Tenjin moto he to itaru hosomichi

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:41.500
It doth lead to the gods in Heaven

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:47.500
Goiken gomuyou toorenu totemo

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:47.500
Thou thoughts matter not for ye cannot pass

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:54.920
Kono ko no too no oiwai ni

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:54.920
To celebrate this child's tenth

00:08:55.430 --> 00:09:01.310
Ryou no ofuda wo osame ni sanzu

00:08:55.430 --> 00:09:01.310
I must make an offering with these talismans

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:07.750
Iki wa yoi nagi, kaeri wa kowaki

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:07.750
The path out is pleasant, but returning is scary

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:14.490
Waga naka kowaki no tooshi kana?

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:14.490
Can I pass despite my fears?

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.320
Toorimase, toorimase

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.320
Let us pass, let us pass

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.280
That's blood!

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:19.780
Will she be okay?

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:21.220
She'll be fine.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:22.520
Kimi won't lose.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:25.490
After all, Kimi has only cried once,

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:26.920
and that was over Tori.

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:31.130
Since Tori's watching, Kimi can't lose.

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:34.840
<i>Excellent! Great!</i>

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:36.770
<i>It feels wonderful,</i>

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:38.840
<i>like everything has been laid open.</i>

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:40.900
<i>But it's not enough;</i>

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.430
<i>it's nothing compared to back then.</i>

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:48.310
It was right after the accident that took Horizon's life.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:51.430
Tori and Horizon were both unconscious

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:53.320
when they were taken to Mikawa,

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.530
but when he came back he was alone...

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.320
He grew thin, unwilling to eat.

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:01.830
Kimi was the one who snapped Tori out of it.

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:05.700
<i>Eat it.</i>

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.290
<i>Sis...</i>

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:10.950
<i>Horizon...</i>

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:14.300
<i>She can't feel anything anymore.</i>

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:23.010
<i>Listen, you aren't Horizon!</i>

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:27.710
<i>Just because Horizon's dead
doesn't mean you have to die too!</i>

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:32.110
<i>Cut it out!</i>

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:31.340
Musashi Salt

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:36.540
<i>He moved!</i>

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:39.740
<i>Tabasco, seven spices and pepper!</i>

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.410
<i>Spices are amazing!</i>

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:44.620
<i>It's true that a grain of pepper is worth a golden coin.</i>

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.330
<i>Go on! Move some more!</i>

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:46.310
Pepper
Seven Spices
Musashi Salt

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.960
<i>Cry out! Cry to your heart's content!</i>

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:52.500
<i>Remember all of your emotions!</i>

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:59.160
<i>Blood and flesh, shuddering and tears...</i>

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:03.040
<i>Regain some of what Horizon has lost.</i>

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:06.670
<i>Are you back?</i>

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:12.690
<i>No, because you never made it
to where Horizon went,</i>

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:14.190
<i>my...</i>

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:16.440
<i>foolish brother!</i>

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:27.090
<i>It will be okay.</i>

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.820
<i>Now listen, from now on, you must live on</i>

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:32.780
<i>like you're crying right now.</i>

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:36.300
<i>Laugh and get angry just like a newborn.</i>

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:39.420
<i>And then help those who can't do that.</i>

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:44.210
<i>You must help others retrieve
the things they were born with</i>

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:46.320
<i>that have been lost or stolen.</i>

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:50.110
<i>I will help you.</i>

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:03.570
That's why no one can stand up to Kimi.

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:06.120
She didn't let Tori leave us.

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:10.540
<i>Right, that was the only time I've ever cried.</i>

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:13.670
<i>This is absolutely nothing compared to then!</i>

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.160
Kimi!

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:31.390
I got through!

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:35.350
Why don't you scream out a wail?

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:47.650
I'm an obscene woman.

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:49.030
Wouldn't you agree?

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:49.700
<i>Damn!</i>

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.490
<i>This question is the Q&A for the dance's intermission!</i>

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:54.920
<i>If I don't answer...</i>

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:57.810
What a pity.

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:00.500
I was hoping you could see what this tastes like.

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:04.590
<i>If I'm no match for her speed...</i>

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:07.520
If you want to fight the outside world,

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:09.970
you must surpass my Slicing Dragonfly first!

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:11.970
Bind, Slicing Dragonfly!

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:25.690
Clueless woman, why the surprise?

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:26.870
But why?!

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:29.530
Doesn't that spear sever its target's name?

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:33.640
A flower's name means nothing to the flower itself.

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:36.380
After all, someone else slapped on its name.

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:37.670
It's the same as fashion.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.720
If you're going to rely on that for your attacks,

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:43.190
you'll have to increase your power level by four digits

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:44.760
if you hope to touch me.

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:47.840
It can't be...

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:49.550
Snap out of it!

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:53.180
You've made a total of three mistakes.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:57.110
Mistake one, you crossed paths with
a magnificent woman like me.

00:13:57.110 --> 00:14:01.360
Magnificent women only lose to their loved ones.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:05.910
Mistake two, speed's your selling point,
yet you tossed it aside

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:09.370
after a dignified lady such as myself
repelled you but once.

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:11.500
Keep attacking and show me what you've got,

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:14.570
even if you know you're no match!

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:21.170
The last mistake is that you are not meant to serve

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:25.090
our cosplaying King of Musashi,

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:27.410
nor the Testament Union,

00:14:27.410 --> 00:14:29.580
nor your half-witted brain,

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:32.570
which decided to side with them for the Far East.

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:33.880
That's...

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:38.850
If you are a Far East samurai,
then it is your duty to serve your lord!

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:42.390
You should be trying to save Horizon!

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:45.320
You're pathetic for having become her enemy!

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:47.650
Now, on your knees! Sit!

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:48.530
Judge!

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:52.320
I over-analyzed things and
nearly made a horrible mistake.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:53.410
You may be licentious,

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:56.160
but I am in debt for your accurate words of advice!

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:59.000
Just so long as you understand.

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:02.200
Foolish brother, do you have anything to say?

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:04.420
Yeah, thanks a whole bunch!

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:08.390
So, what now?

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:10.370
I won the fight.

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:12.020
<i>Indeed!</i>

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:13.350
<i>Now what will you do? Well?</i>

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:17.060
<i>If Tori Aoi becomes king of Musashi,</i>

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:21.060
<i>Musashi will probably be freed from its constraints.</i>

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:23.310
<i>But the Testament Union will view him as a threat</i>

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:26.370
<i>and justifiably declare him hostile.</i>

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:29.460
King of Musashi, don't worry.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:33.570
A king's gotta stand proud, right?

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:35.230
Or what?

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:42.410
As promised, Ic shall return

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:45.290
authority to the Supreme Federation and Student Council.

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:50.340
But Ic cannot transfer my kingship.

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:54.520
This will stand true even if Princess Horizon returns.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:57.390
Musashi will keep me as its king in line

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:00.980
with the Testament Union's dispatch.

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:03.210
<i>Obviously!</i>

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:04.730
However!

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:08.030
Ic shall appoint two viceroys as my assistants.

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:12.350
Next, Ic shall split their power by
giving them one privilege each.

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:18.240
Ic hereby appoint Horizon Ariadust
and Tori Aoi as my viceroys!

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:20.620
<i>Have you gone mad, King of Musashi?!</i>

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:24.460
Your Holiness, Ic am the King of Musashi.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:27.970
As king, Ic must always stay with my people

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:32.700
and help them through their suffering and strife.

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:36.730
If you believe my actions are harmful
to the Testament Union,

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:38.480
we can pass judgment at the next

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:40.350
Testament Union Conference of Representatives.

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:43.770
<i>The Testament Union Conference of Representatives
is an international affair.</i>

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:46.710
<i>The Testament does not mention any conferences</i>

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:49.450
<i>like this in our current era.</i>

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.030
No, it does!

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:53.570
There's the Peace of Westphalia.

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:57.120
The meeting that peacefully ended
the Thirty Years' War

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.620
and led to several new international laws

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.450
will be held in half a year, on October 24th.

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:04.120
What do you say?

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:05.860
Why don't we use that conference

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:08.820
to weigh the future of Musashi and the Far East?

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:12.420
<i>But that means you will war against</i>

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:15.340
<i>the Testament Union until that conference!</i>

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:18.240
We can hold out if the end is in sight.

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:22.800
Our job is to go to Westphalia,

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:24.440
retrieve the Armors of Deadly Sins,

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:26.440
and save the world from annihilation!

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:30.400
I would like the Armors to go back
to their rightful owner.

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:34.460
<i>As a representative of the Testament Union,</i>

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:36.780
<i>I feel Musashi's decision is dangerous.</i>

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:39.730
<i>As such, we shall proceed with our plans</i>

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:43.660
<i>to abstract the Armor from
Horizon Ariadust after her suicide.</i>

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:45.930
<i>And we shall proceed with relocating </i>

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:48.790
<i>the people of Musashi to revive Mikawa.</i>

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.130
Got it!

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:53.810
Well, you take care of that.

00:17:53.810 --> 00:17:55.760
I'm gonna go tell Horizon how I feel.

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:56.840
<i>You bastard!</i>

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.530
What's your problem, Geezer?!

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:00.900
What the hell do you think you're doing?!

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:04.730
You've captured my beloved Horizon (to be)
and wanna execute her?!

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:05.770
You jerks!

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:07.750
You've stripped Horizon naked,

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:09.790
chained her down and stolen her freedom.

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:08.790
Censored

00:18:09.790 --> 00:18:11.470
Then, you tortured her, condemned her

00:18:11.470 --> 00:18:13.780
or did somethin' wet and messy, didn't you?

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:15.190
<i>Hell no!</i>

00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:18.260
<i>There's no point in any further conversation.</i>

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:20.620
<i>We shall proceed as planned.</i>

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:22.250
<i>If you wish to intervene,</i>

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:25.360
<i>there will be student contention as
dictated in the school rules.</i>

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:27.220
Huh?!

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:33.630
The side fighting for Musashi Ariadust
Academy was victorious.

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:37.700
As sanctioned by witness of the Testament Union,

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:41.140
the Far East has decided to rescue Horizon Ariadust.

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:44.290
Rescue! Rescue!

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:47.020
Well then, I best be off.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:53.070
You guys taught me that we stand
a chance of rescuing Horizon.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:56.620
Horizon isn't a human only meant to die.

00:18:56.620 --> 00:19:00.280
You taught me that she wasn't born just to die.

00:19:00.670 --> 00:19:02.870
So, I'll be going now.

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:06.600
But you don't have to go along with this anymore,

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:08.590
since I'm just doing what I want.

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:12.380
But if someone you care for is
ever in the eyes of danger,

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:14.350
don't hesitate to save him.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:16.550
You can do it.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:18.920
As someone inept, you have my guarantee!

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:20.450
<i>The fool...</i>

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:24.560
<i>He's doing the exact same thing that Ic did once.</i>

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:30.640
<i>Ic once believed that my land would be saved if Ic left.</i>

00:19:30.970 --> 00:19:33.260
<i>But one person can't...</i>

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:38.990
You're going with him?

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:43.490
Oh, I should put these guys back, huh?

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:48.200
That is my country's crest!

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:51.710
Adele, where did you get that spear?

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:53.320
Oh, this?

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:56.020
My father left it for me to use as I saw fit.

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:57.280
Your father did?

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:01.930
Right, a long time ago,
my father lived in a foreign country.

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:03.760
Supposedly, their king surrendered

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:08.270
himself to the Testament Union in exchange for peace.

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:10.970
My father felt that the king sold himself

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:13.500
because the people weren't doing their part.

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:17.480
He thought everyone should have
been more courageous.

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:20.980
So when he gave me this spear,
he told me to make sure

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:22.240
to protect my king.

00:20:23.020 --> 00:20:25.190
I see...

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:28.150
What are you going to do now?

00:20:28.150 --> 00:20:29.260
Judge!

00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:31.540
I am going to go protect our king!

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:33.800
Nate, I'm countin' on ya!

00:20:34.190 --> 00:20:37.030
Remember that old promise, Madam Knight?

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:40.380
You never forget the past!

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:42.170
I fully remember, my king.

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:46.260
The time for me to show you
my strength as a knight has come.

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:49.760
You find them more intriguing than us, Masazumi?

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:52.140
You wanted to be hands-on, didn't you?

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:57.950
My arms itch for action!

00:20:57.950 --> 00:20:59.190
Y..Your arms?

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:02.280
I swear, we're a close bunch.

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:04.030
Hey, now, Azuma!

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:05.530
Are you sure you should go?

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:06.960
I'll be fine.

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:09.160
I'm sure I can do something to help.

00:21:10.090 --> 00:21:11.610
Good luck, everyone.

00:21:11.610 --> 00:21:12.660
I'll be waiting.

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:19.040
Good luck, good luck!

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:23.890
Neshinbara, please contact the Guard
and come up with a strategy.

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:25.610
Sponsor: Neshinbara
Kitano Tenmangu Shrine

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:25.630
Judge!

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:29.920
Asama, say, could you prepare to pass that through?

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:33.730
Foolish brother, you aren't forgetting
something important now are you?

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:35.780
It's all good, sis!

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:37.770
I'll never give up on life ever again.

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:39.280
So please!

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:42.240
You probably wouldn't listen if I refused anyway.

00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:43.240
Thanks!

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:44.860
Hey, Futayo.

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:45.740
What is it?

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:50.070
Enroll in our school as the temporary vice chancellor.

00:21:50.070 --> 00:21:53.100
I am a samurai and not a noble,

00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:55.870
so it is my job to protect my master, Lady Horizon.

00:21:56.440 --> 00:21:58.230
But if that does not bother you...

00:21:58.230 --> 00:21:59.500
That's cool.

00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:01.500
Yo!

00:22:02.890 --> 00:22:05.040
I sent a copy to you.

00:22:04.470 --> 00:22:06.840
Letter of Recommendation for School Enrollment
Horizon Ariadust

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:08.970
Be sure everyone, including Horizon, makes it back.

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:11.990
Listen up!

00:22:11.990 --> 00:22:15.210
Don't do your best; don't endeavor.

00:22:15.210 --> 00:22:19.530
Simply use all of the power and
strength you've built up.

00:22:19.530 --> 00:22:20.900
And if that isn't enough...

00:22:22.760 --> 00:22:23.900
come back alive.

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:25.030
Judge!

00:22:26.680 --> 00:22:28.740
<i>I'm going to become king!</i>

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:31.240
<i>I'm going to become king of a country where </i>

00:22:31.240 --> 00:22:32.900
<i>everyone's dreams come true.</i>

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:37.330
<i>I'm going to become king of a country where Horizon can</i>

00:22:37.330 --> 00:22:39.290
<i>have her dreams!</i>

00:22:39.820 --> 00:22:41.500
C'mon, let's go, everybody!

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:43.700
I'm counting on you.

00:22:43.700 --> 00:22:44.420
Judge!

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:50.260
Sora ni nozomu you ni

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:50.260
Our voyage across the real world

00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:57.270
Koukai suru genjitsu sekai no tabi

00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:57.270
Is like navigating straight for the sky

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.610
Nani mo mottenai kedo

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.610
I may not have anything

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.720
Kokoro no naka

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.720
But I have a dream

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:08.950
Kagayaita yume ga aru yo

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:08.950
That's shone brightly in my heart

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.790
Mada kikoenai

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.790
I still haven't heard

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:15.280
Kimi no hontou no mune no koe

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:15.280
The voice spoken from your heart

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:20.200
Shiritain da — sugao wo misete yo

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:20.200
Let me in — show me the real you

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:23.790
Barabara ni chirabatta

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:23.790
We'll bury the void

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:26.890
Ikutsu mo no piisu wo

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:26.890
As we find all of the pieces

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:29.560
Hitotsu zutsu sagashite

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:29.560
That have gotten scattered around

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.720
Kuuhaku wo umete iku no sa

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.720
One piece at a time

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:37.540
Ubawareta kimi no egao

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:37.540
Your smile has been stolen

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:41.210
Tori modosu tame ni hashiru yo

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:41.210
But I will race to get it back

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:47.150
Boku wa hikari sasu michi wo

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:47.150
As I run down the shining path

00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:10.990
Next Episode
The Trumpeter at the Start Line
